<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32601" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπεράω</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			Arc.
		</span></i>
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσ-</span></b> , v. infr.<i><span class="en">
			1.4
		</span></i>), 
			Ep.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπεράασκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.381
				</span></i>
			:— <i>go out over, pass beyond,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαῖτμα μέγ᾽ ἐκπερόωσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.35
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥ τ᾽ ἐκπεράᾳ μέγα λαῖτμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.323
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					713
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλῶνα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				731
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέρσον καὶ θάλασσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					240
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. βίον</span>
			<i>go through</i> life, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				18
			</span></i> (anap.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀγδώκοντ᾽ ἔτεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.226
				</span></i>
			(<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα συμφορᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					824
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs., of an
			arrow, <i>pass through, pierce,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊστὸς ἀντικρὺ..ὑπ᾽ ὀστέον
					ἐξεπέρησεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.652
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.346
			</span></i>, etc.; of persons, <i>go forth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				6.18
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθήνας</span> to Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				10.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>go</i> or <i>come out of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελάθρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					512
				</span></i>
			(lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>transgress,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσπερᾶσαι πὰρ ἃν λέγῃ ἱεροθύτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(2).6
				</span></i>
			 (Tegea, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>carry out</i> or <i>away,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Nu.</u>
				11.31
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
